/**
\page devs_genproc GenProc DEVS coupled model

\tableofcontents

\section genproc_overview Overview

Generator feeding a single-server JobProcessor. The external `stop` input is
routed to the generator; the processor's `out` port is re-exported as the
coupled model's `out`.

| | |
|---|---|
| Kind | Coupled DEVS model |
| Formalism | Parallel DEVS (PythonPDEVS) |
| Language / framework | Python / PythonPDEVS (pypdevs) |
| Source | `gen_proc.py` ( \ref gen_proc.GenProc ) |
| Parameters | `name` (default `"GenProc"`), `period` (default 2.0), `processing_time` (default 1.0) |

\section genproc_formal Formal specification

    N = < X, Y, D, {M_d}, EIC, IC, EOC >

- X = external input ports { stop }
- Y = external output ports { out }
- D = { gen, proc }
- M_d, EIC, IC and EOC are tabulated in the sections below.
- No Select function: PythonPDEVS is a Parallel DEVS simulator, so simultaneous
  events are resolved by the components' confluent transitions.

\section genproc_ports Ports

\subsection genproc_inports External input ports

| Port | Value type | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `stop` | any | forwarded to the generator; any message stops job generation |

\subsection genproc_outports External output ports

| Port | Value type | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `out` | `Job` | finished jobs leaving the processor |

\section genproc_components Components (D and M_d)

| Component | Model | Kind | Parameters | Specification |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `gen` | Generator | atomic | period | \subpage devs_generator |
| `proc` | JobProcessor | atomic | processing_time | \subpage devs_jobprocessor |

\section genproc_couplings Couplings

\subsection genproc_eic External input couplings (EIC)

| Coupled port | Component | Component port |
|---|---|---|
| `stop` | `gen` | `stop` |

\subsection genproc_ic Internal couplings (IC)

| From component | From port | To component | To port |
|---|---|---|---|
| `gen` | `out` | `proc` | `in` |

\subsection genproc_eoc External output couplings (EOC)

| Component | Component port | Coupled port |
|---|---|---|
| `proc` | `out` | `out` |

\section genproc_diagram Coupling diagram

\dot
digraph genproc_couplings {
    rankdir=LR;
    node [fontname="Helvetica", fontsize=10];
    edge [fontname="Helvetica", fontsize=9];
    subgraph cluster_genproc {
        label="GenProc";
        style=rounded;
        gen [shape=box, label="gen : Generator"];
        proc [shape=box, label="proc : JobProcessor"];
    }
    in_stop [shape=plaintext, label="stop"];
    out_out [shape=plaintext, label="out"];
    in_stop -> gen [label="stop -> stop"];
    gen -> proc [label="out -> in"];
    proc -> out_out [label="out -> out"];
}
\enddot

\section genproc_sequence Typical interaction

Every `period` the generator emits a job; the processor serves it for
`processing_time` and forwards it; a `stop` from the environment silences the
generator. With the defaults (period 2.0, processing_time 1.0) no job is ever
dropped.

\msc
    hscale = "1.6";
    env [label="environment"], gen [label="gen : Generator"], proc [label="proc : JobProcessor"], out [label="GenProc.out"];
    gen->proc [label="out -> in : Job(k)"];
    proc->proc [label="busy, ta = processing_time"];
    proc->out [label="out -> out : Job(k)"];
    env->gen [label="stop -> stop"];
    gen->gen [label="passive, ta = inf"];
\endmsc

\section genproc_source Source mapping

| Element | Implementation in `gen_proc.py` |
|---|---|
| Ports | \ref gen_proc.GenProc.stop "GenProc.stop", \ref gen_proc.GenProc.out "GenProc.out" via `addInPort` / `addOutPort` |
| Components | \ref gen_proc.GenProc.gen "GenProc.gen", \ref gen_proc.GenProc.proc "GenProc.proc" via `addSubModel` |
| Couplings | three `connectPorts` calls in \ref gen_proc.GenProc.__init__ "GenProc.__init__()" |
*/
